While debugging my telnetTiles program on NAO, I started up a random 
character.  So what does it give me?  A chaotic female human wizard.  I 
just had to laugh.  As anyone checking my record on NAO can see 
(username:Myrddin), wizards are my most ascended character.  If I just 
want a relaxing game, I go for gnomish wizards, and ascend a relatively 
high percentage of them.

So I relaxed into it, smoky potions were confusion, alas.  Minetown 
altar was coaligned, so after credit cloning a decent AC, sacfested 
there until Anhur grudgingly coughed up MagicBane.  Went down one level, 
found a grey stone on a recently departed dwarf.  The poor soul got in 
the way of my 'testing' an attack spell.  Repeatedly.  :)  Kick tested 
as safe, I picked it up and price id-ed it upstairs as a luckstone, so I 
decided to just go on to Soko.

While credit cloning, I noticed one of the rings was a cursed mid range 
expensive ring.  During a particularly awkward fight, this knowledge 
came in handy.  Anhur was still being stingy at that point, so I was 
using my fingers for E-wording.  With my HP low, prayer timeout not yet 
expired, and no ID-ed teleportation scrolls handy, I noted that my Exp 
level was 8, just high enough for a wizard to willingly teleport, if he 
had teleportitus.  I donned the ring, crossed my fingers, and hit ctrl-T 
... *bamf!*  Yay!  Live to fight another day!  And this scroll marked 
enchant armor or remove curse is ... remove curse.  So I take off the ring.

By the time I got to the top of Soko, (the amulet version), my backpack 
was getting full repeatedly.  An elf dropped an amulet, and after 
looking in across the zoo to make sure that all the doors were open, I 
surmised that it was the AoR.  My AC was single digit negative, which is 
  midway between panic and comfortable.  (10 is "Run away!  Run away!", 
5 is PANIC, 0 is "I can breathe, now.", -10 is comfortable, -20 is 
beefy, -30 is "Dances with minotaurs")  The next thing on my list of 
wants was a bag of holding, and spellbooks.  At that point, I remembered 
that I hadn't fully explored the mines yet.  Hmmm.

Since I was playing a wizard, I was a little more relaxed about how I 
was playing.  Hence, I gambled, and lost, about eating a tengu corpse. 
Teleportitus.  Crap!  Then, while in a main level shop, I carelessly 
picked up something to mark it's price, and *bamf*... oops.  Take a 
step, kill a Kop.  Another step, another Kop.  Yawn.  Even with -4 AC, 
they aren't much more than speed bumps.  Finally wade back to the shop, 
and throw enough money at the problem to make it go away.  But that's 
not why I nearly quit.  No, that comes later.

On the second level of the mines below the town, a random bag lying on 
the ground is a bag of holding.  I chuckle.  The RNG taketh away, the 
RNG giveth.  I keep exploring, in search of more spellbooks.  I wanted 
identify.  The next level is a bones level.  Kinda wierd, it was a 
fellow wizard who got offed by a leocrotta, but I never saw the beast. 
Huh.  But he had a magic marker.  Another level down, another bones 
file, another marker.  Hee hee.  Another level down, the maze of the 
mines.  Yay!  Spellbooks!  Between these, the minetown bookshop, and the 
oracle level, I had a screenful of spells going into the midgame.

A huge throne room in the main dungeon, a few levels below the soko 
branch had a silver dragon in it, who dropped scales.  This elevated my 
ac into the "beefy" range, and I sat on the throne with all my money in 
inventory.  I... sat!  on the throne!  with *ALL* my money!  IN 
INVENTORY!  First sit: "You notice you have no gold!  The throne 
vanishes is a puff of (spiteful) logic"  But that wasn't where I felt 
like #quitting.  Nope, that's later.

A few levels after discovering the quest portal (and trying without 
success to gain control over my teleporting via the guaranteed tengu 
there), I found a graveyard, which boosted my Exp level to 14, so I went 
back up to complete the quest.  On the quest, a tengu corpse *finally* 
left me feeling in control of myself.

Then I dip tested a potion I found in the Dark One's domain.  'U - a 
whistle'  Argh.  Polymorph.  Right.  But that wasn't where I felt like 
#quitting.  Yep.  You guessed it.  Later.

Wiped the Dark One, got the Eye, then went to scour the dungeon for a 
replacement unicorn horn.  Found one, then went down to the castle with 
little happening.  Didn't find Ludious, but didn't look real hard, either.

By the time I made it to the castle, I had nearly my whole kit. 
Reflection, multiple sources of MR, a Robe, perma invis, teleport and 
control, slow digestion, tinning kit and can of grease, 2 magic markers, 
spellbooks of ID, mapping, and detect treasure (all written), plenty low 
AC in the "Dances with Minotaurs" range, jumping boots (a great toy).  I 
opened the drawbridge with a wand of opening, only for a soldier to 
smash it to bits first move with a wand of striking.  Aw.  I rained down 
death upon all their heads, taking time to snatch the wand, check the 
armory, and gobble on a black dragon corpse.  I used my intrinsic 
teleportation on the castle level as a way to control my satiation.  I 
was missing free action and wanted charm monster, but decided to search 
the rest of the dungeon before breaking the wishless conduct, so I 
stashed the wand.  I magic-mapped, detect-trasured, detect-monstered the 
whole of Gehennom, courtesy of the eye's magic regen.  That's why I love 
wizards so much.  On the level I found Vlad's, I still hadn't found any 
additional kit, so I took out one of the scrolls of genocide I found 
earlier and blessed it.  Do you know what I nuked?  Liches?  Nah, with 
Magicbane, they're just an amusement.  Mindflayers?  Magic missile them 
to death.  Eels?  At Exp Level 15, I gained intrinsic warning, and I 
could always cast detect monsters, so they didn't bother me.  No, I 
genocided 'm'.
With all the mimics gone before Orcus' town was generated, each shop was 
filled with random loot.  None of it good, naturally, but the *plan* was 
  a good one.
Quickly made it to the bottom of Gehennom, and found the square.  Dug 
out everywhere around it, and cast light to mark the location.  By this 
time, I had two remaining pet shades, so I went up one level to the wiz 
portal, and cleared that out to the top.  I looked myself over, and 
realized I lacked free action, but that was about it.  So I zapped a 
hole in the wall, Rodney teleported next to me, and summoned a purple & 
right away.  Gulp.
Slow down.  Do.  Not.  Move.  Hit ';'.  Look at ... 'Yeenoghu'.  Oh. 
Ok, back to normal speed.  Jump to the door, jump in the room.  Give 
Rodney a taste of Orcus' wand.  Stab Yeenoghu to death.  Summon pets 
next to me and read cursed scroll to bottom of mines.  *Bamf* lit spot. 
   Candle.  Bell.  Book.  Go down, burn Elbereth.  Time for some last 
minute preparations, now that the last level has been generated. 
Enchant up Magicbane to +7.  Wield the throwing daggers, enchant them up 
to +5.  Hmm.  Need another enchant weapon scroll.  Pull it out, and ...
switch back to stab some random critter that was disturbing me.  Then 
read the enchant weapon scroll (after blessing it, of course!)
"Your MagicBane glows violently silver, and evaporates!"
This, of course, is where I had a nervous breakdown, and nearly quit. 
I'd *ALREADY* killed the wizard, you see, and Magicbane was the only 
artifact weapon I'd had (well, ok, Sting, and Trollsbane, I think, but 
seriously)  What was I left with?!  6 +5 slightly rusty daggers.  *Whimper*

I slowly collected myself, and killed everything in sight.  Until I made 
it to the inner sanctum.  Zap magic missile at high priest.  Moloch 
throws his two cents in with a lightning bolt.  Zap again, Moloch again. 
  High priest makes it next to me, and so I check my progress with a 
stethoscope.  139/139?!  Aw crap.  He was generated with a cloak of MR. 
  And, apparently, he's not hurt by lightning anymore.  This could be 
scary.  I check my arsenal.  Yep.  All 6 +5 rusty daggers, still there. 
  I jump around him like mad, throwing daggers at him, holding one back 
to tickle him with when he approaches, before jumping to safety again. 
All the while, Moloch is roaring and zapping us both ineffectually. 
Finally, the High Priest succumbs, and I high tail it out of there.

Being chaotic, the mysterious force isn't too irritating, and I climb up 
to a dlvl 11 altar tucked in a corner.  I decide that I don't have 
confidence in 6 +5 rusty corroded daggers to get the job done, and want 
an artifact weapon.

Anhur: "Dance!  Dance!  Sucker!"

I get crowned, but Anhur gives me a FoD spellbook.  Fine.  Hundreds of 
create monster castings later, I feel reconciled after being crowned.
Then I create monster, stab, check the loot, step back, cast.
Then I stab, check the loot, step back, cast.
Then I stab, check the loot, step back, cast.
...
...
...
Repeat hundreds of times, to Anhur's amusement.
A ki-rin steps around the boulder wall I made.
A ki-rin?!  Randomly generated?!  WOW.  Check his level... 16.  Hmm, I'm 
22 now.  *bamf* to the upstairs, up one level, wish for charm monster 
spellbook.  read.  throw it away.  down, *bamf*
"*So* nice to meet you!"  First cast, a tame ki-rin.  Wish number 3, a 
saddle.  Saddle up the ki-rin, but don't mount yet, as I still haven't 
gotten an arti weapon.
A few sacs later.  A purple 'A' steps around the corner.  A randomly 
generated ARCHON?!  Holy @#$@.  Put on blindfold.  "nice to ... meet 
you?"  A tame Archon.  With the long sword named Sunsword.  Oh, suuuure, 
   *he* gets an artifact weapon.  *grumble*

More sacs.  "Use my gift wisely."  FINALLY.  About time that stingy 
deity granted me... *DRAGONBANE*?!  That sonofa.

More soul draining sacs.  Even more.  More after that.  "Use my gift 
wisely."  Frostbrand.  Whew.

Here's a saddle, that means the ki-rin picked a fight he couldn't 
handle.  Fine.  recharged, and wished for a replacement figurine.

Did anyone know that a hasted ki-rin mount on the Plane of Air is a 
beautiful thing?  I could actually avoid air elementals there!  Didn't 
get engulfed once.

On Fire, my ki-rin picked a fight with a fire vortex.  And burned 
himself.  Repeatedly.  Poof, second dead ki-rin.  5th wish, new ki-rin 
mount.

On Astral, had to visit all three altars, but was fun.  I killed Pesty 
once on the way in, then used tricky jumping on the way out.  Famine got 
in my way, so he went down to a wand of death, then was jumped around.

Death... never made it near me.

You ascend to the status of Demigoddess...

Myrddin, chaotic female human Wizard




